blocks.text:
Good news first: for a habit or a state over a long period, the **past simple is also correct**. *When I was a child, I lived in Bandung* and *When I was a child, I used to live in Bandung* are both fine. used to just makes it clearer that it's **not true any more**.

But used to means **'again and again' or 'for a long time'**, so it **can't** be used for:
- **one event**: *I went to Bali last year* (one trip), not 'I used to go to Bali last year';
- **a total number of times**: *I visited Japan three times*;
- **a specific moment**: *yesterday, last Saturday, two days ago, in 2015, at 7 o'clock*.

Careful: **three times a year**, **every Friday**, **on Sundays** describe a habit, so used to is fine: *I used to go to Bali three times a year.*

id.text:
Kabar baik dulu: untuk kebiasaan atau keadaan dalam waktu yang lama, **past simple juga benar**. *When I was a child, I lived in Bandung* dan *When I was a child, I used to live in Bandung* sama-sama benar. used to hanya membuat lebih jelas bahwa hal itu **sekarang sudah tidak lagi**.

Tapi used to artinya **'berulang-ulang' atau 'dalam waktu lama'**, jadi **tidak bisa** dipakai untuk:
- **satu kejadian**: *I went to Bali last year* (satu kali liburan), bukan 'I used to go to Bali last year';
- **jumlah kali secara total**: *I visited Japan three times*;
- **waktu tertentu**: *yesterday, last Saturday, two days ago, in 2015, at 7 o'clock*.

Hati-hati: **three times a year** (tiga kali setahun), **every Friday**, **on Sundays** itu kebiasaan, jadi used to boleh: *I used to go to Bali three times a year.*
